  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If a transform is animated to one position/rotation but it also has a constraint controlling it to a different position/rotation, then physbones will behave as though they are at the animated position/rotation, while visually the object will be at the constrained position/rotation. This also affects eye look/tracking, if the transform in question is a parent of the eye bones and you have the debug visuals on. \n\nHere is an avatar where the eye tracking symptom is clearly visible:  avtr_ba3daad5-0c64-4fb4-8593-38265acd9ad3\n\nI should mention that this also affects both unity constraints and vrc constraints, but I mention it here because now with the VRC Constraints there is a possibility of this finally being fixed.",
